{
  "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition is centered with generous negative space, captured from a 3/4 overhead angle (40-degree) to showcase the volume and texture of two rustic, shallow ceramic bowls. One bowl is in sharp focus in the foreground, while the second is slightly softened in the background. Shallow depth of field creates a beautiful, natural bokeh. Soft, natural light streams from a window on the left, casting gentle shadows and highlighting the glistening sheen of olive oil on the food. The setting is a worn, rustic oak tabletop with natural wood grain. Props include a single wooden spoon resting naturally beside the front bowl and a few stray, vibrant green baby spinach leaves and a dusting of hemp hearts scattered on the wood. The dish features a hearty mixture of farro grains and tender, wilted baby spinach, interspersed with halved cherry tomatoes that show soft, blistered skins and exposed, juicy interiors with visible seeds. Softly scrambled, creamy yellow eggs are folded throughout the mixture. The colors are earthy: warm amber tones from the farro, bright pops of red from the tomato segments, and deep forest green from the wilted spinach, all finished with a light dusting of black pepper and red chili flakes. The final assembly looks like a nutritious, home-cooked meal for two. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene reflects a lived-in, warm kitchen atmosphere. Include subtle, authentic details like a tiny smudge of olive oil on the table surface, an asymmetric garnish of hemp hearts, and natural, uneven textures of the scrambled eggs. Warm, golden-hour color temperature, cozy and inviting. No text, no watermarks, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional editorial food photography."
}
